  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "usage",
      "title": "vil ha, takk, bare hyggelig",
      "text": "\"Vil du ha …?\" is the everyday way to offer something: word for word \"will you have …?\". \"Jeg vil ha …\" is \"I want …\", and it is not rude. A question puts the verb first: \"Vil du ha kaffe?\". \"Takk\" is \"thanks\" and \"Bare hyggelig\" (\"just pleasant\") is a common answer to it.",
